From: xob0t <32616886+xob0t@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:58:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/22] Name Array::NewSpecific and Object::New /
 NewAllocSpecific in signature libraries

Whole-program optimized code inlines SZArrayNew and il2cpp_codegen_object_new and
calls the runtime's allocators behind them: Array::NewSpecific(klass, length),
Object::New(klass) and Object::NewAllocSpecific(klass). No helper rule named
them, so no library could hold them and those calls stayed unidentified native
calls ("Klass value used as data"). They are now SzArrayNew and ObjectNew when a
library is built from symbols. The shipped libraries are unchanged until they
are rebuilt.

A 6000.0.60f1 library rebuilt with this from four test builds (Master, Release,
Master for size, Master without incremental GC; MSVC 14.50) names the game's
NewSpecific and NewAllocSpecific; 0 wrong identifications on each build, in
sample and held out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Rewind.Analysis/Runtime/RuntimeHelpers.cs | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Rewind.Analysis/Runtime/RuntimeHelpers.cs b/src/Rewind.Analysis/Runtime/RuntimeHelpers.cs
index aee68c7..281c42c 100644
--- a/src/Rewind.Analysis/Runtime/RuntimeHelpers.cs
+++ b/src/Rewind.Analysis/Runtime/RuntimeHelpers.cs
@@ -297,6 +297,11 @@ public sealed class RuntimeHelpers
         // Its overload with a class to check against is something else.
         if (name == "?UnBox@@YAPEAXPEAUIl2CppObject@@@Z") return new HelperInfo(HelperKind.Unbox, 1, false, true, name);
         if (core == "il2cpp_codegen_resolve") return new HelperInfo(HelperKind.ResolvePInvoke, 1, false, true, name);
+        // The runtime's allocators behind SZArrayNew and il2cpp_codegen_object_new, which whole-program optimized
+        // code calls directly once the codegen wrapper is inlined: Array::NewSpecific(klass, length),
+        // Object::New(klass) and Object::NewAllocSpecific(klass).
+        if (core == "NewSpecific@Array@vm@il2cpp") return new HelperInfo(HelperKind.SzArrayNew, 2, false, true, name);
+        if (core is "New@Object@vm@il2cpp" or "NewAllocSpecific@Object@vm@il2cpp") return new HelperInfo(HelperKind.ObjectNew, 1, false, true, name);
         if (core is "IsInstClass" or "IsInstSealed") return new HelperInfo(HelperKind.IsInst, 2, false, true, name);
         // (Plain Castclass - any class or interface - is pasted in place by MSVC, but clang keeps it a function.)
         if (core is "CastclassClass" or "CastclassSealed" or "Castclass") return new HelperInfo(HelperKind.CastClass, 2, false, true, name);
